Description: pvr: hold render state and render info once per split sub command
 A dynamic render can be split into several graphics sub commands: at the end
 of transform feedback (CmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT, and the mid-fragment
 barrier in pvr_xfb_end()), at the barrier event of
 vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT, at stencil store/load barriers and when the
 occlusion query pool changes. pvr_arch_cmd_buffer_start_sub_cmd() gives
 each of them the render state and the render info of the render.
 .
 Freeing a sub command drops one reference on the render state
 (pvr_render_state_cache_put()), but vkCmdBeginRendering takes only one. With
 zink every transform feedback draw ends with CmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT, so
 the reference count underflows, the render state goes back to the idle list
 or is destroyed while later sub commands and command buffers still use it.
 Before the render state cache, pvr_rstate_entry_remove() searched the device
 list and did nothing the second time.
 .
 The render info had the same problem in the splits without an explicit
 hand-over (barrier event, query pool change): each sub command destroyed it,
 a double free. GL-CTS KHR-GL31.transform_feedback.draw_xfb_test
 (glDrawTransformFeedback after paused and resumed transform feedback) runs
 through both paths and ends with a segmentation fault.
 .
 Take a render state reference for each owned graphics sub command of a
 dynamic render and move the render info to the newest one when it starts.
 vkCmdBeginRendering drops its own reference once its sub command holds one.
 The explicit hand-overs in the transform feedback and mid-fragment barrier
 paths are covered by this and removed. Secondary command buffers that
 continue a render pass are unchanged, they do not free either.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
